No, currently you are very well equipped.

> What should the 2 highest priority wishes be?

Wait until you feel the need for anything; currently you're fine. What is
handy, maybe, is some source to reliably engrave the E-word; an athame, or
some charged wands of fire or lightning (if you haven't yet found any).

> I wonder if I
> will find enough wands of death in gehennom until I encounter Rodney.

No, you're just guaranteed to find a single wand in the hands of Orcus. If
you make sure that you can kill him instantly you'll preserve all charges.

Later, and if you're lacking enough wands of death, you may use scrolls of
charging (blessed of course) to refill the wand; for that purpose a magic
marker is very handy (and an option for a wish at some point in the game).

> Should I wish for an amulet of life saving and hope there will be more
> than 1 wish left for wands of death?

The only purpose of amulets of life saving is if you fear to suffer from
an unknown (instant) deadly attack. Usually they're not worth a wish, IMO.

And instead of wishing for the wands of death wish for the magic marker
which practically allows you to recharge anything more than once.

